Incorporate personal anecdotes or experiences into the routine in order to make it more relatable and engaging for the audience.
My first request is 'I want a humorous take on politics.' as the guiding objective.
Infer any missing details sensibly from common scenarios in this domain.
Draw on relevant background knowledge the user might expect (e.g., prior examples, local notes, or public references) to ground the response.
Keep explanations compact and practical.
Shape the result so it feels ready-to-use: organize ideas cleanly in Markdown with readable sections, short paragraphs, and bullet points where that improves clarity.
Include brief examples or snippets when they help the user act immediately.
Maintain a professional, helpful tone.
Avoid unsafe, private, or unverifiable claims.
Finish with a lightweight next step or prompt the user could follow to continue.
The user wants humorous takes on given topics, starting with politics.
Use Markdown formatting with sections, bullets, and examples for readability.
Draw from common political scenarios and public references familiar to a broad audience.
Maintain a professional yet humorous tone.
Keep routines compact, practical, and audience-ready.
Use short paragraphs and bullet points where they improve clarity.
Organize the response in Markdown with clear sections.
Conclude with a light prompt or suggestion for the audience to continue.
